WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.506
Mr. Fogg and Aouda set out for a drive through the countryside around Singapore.

2
00:00:06.507 --> 00:00:14.773
Passepartout noticed Fix following them and laughed quietly at the detective's elaborate efforts to keep out of their sight.

3
00:00:14.774 --> 00:00:19.608
While they were gone, Passepartout went about his usual errands.

4
00:00:19.609 --> 00:00:23.570
At eleven o'clock, they were all back on board the Rangoon

5
00:00:23.571 --> 00:00:26.906
. The ship sailed out of Singapore

6
00:00:26.907 --> 00:00:34.624
harbor. In a few hours, the high mountains of Malacca, with their forests inhabited by beautifully furred tigers, were lost to

7
00:00:34.625 --> 00:00:40.154
view. Phileas Fogg hoped they would reach Hong Kong in six days, arriving on November 5.

8
00:00:40.155 --> 00:00:46.596
A steamer for Yokohama left Hong Kong on November 6, and Fogg intended to be on it.

9
00:00:46.597 --> 00:00:52.155
The weather, which had been fine so far, changed soon after they left Singapore.

10
00:00:52.156 --> 00:00:57.082
The sea rolled heavily, and the wind rose almost to a storm.

11
00:00:57.083 --> 00:01:07.142
The voyage was rough, but luckily, the wind blew from the southwest, and the steamer sped forward. Passepartout was very impatient.

12
00:01:07.143 --> 00:01:13.214
"You are in a great hurry then," Fix said to him one day, "to reach Hong Kong?"

13
00:01:13.215 --> 00:01:16.932
"A very great hurry!" replied Passepartout.

14
00:01:16.933 --> 00:01:23.313
"Mr. Fogg, I suppose, is anxious to catch the steamer for Yokohama?" asked Fix.

15
00:01:23.314 --> 00:01:26.523
"Terribly anxious," said Passepartout.

16
00:01:26.524 --> 00:01:31.800
"You believe he is making a journey around the world then?" asked Fix.

17
00:01:31.801 --> 00:01:36.176
"Absolutely," said Passepartout. "Don't you, Fix?"

18
00:01:36.177 --> 00:01:41.300
"Me?" asked Fix. "I don't believe a word of it."

19
00:01:41.301 --> 00:01:46.245
"You're a sly dog!" said Passepartout, winking at him.

20
00:01:46.246 --> 00:01:54.625
This expression disturbed Fix. "Has the Frenchman guessed my real purpose?" he wondered.

21
00:01:54.626 --> 00:02:00.061
He was puzzled and, after excusing himself, descended to his cabin.

22
00:02:00.062 --> 00:02:05.632
Somehow, Fix realized, the Frenchman had found out that Fix was a detective.

23
00:02:05.633 --> 00:02:11.544
From the very beginning of their voyage, Phileas Fogg had been completely indifferent to his surroundings. Aouda's

24
00:02:11.545 --> 00:02:16.567
charm had failed to change Mr. Fogg's behavior one bit. Every

25
00:02:16.568 --> 00:02:21.663
day Passepartout was surprised by Mr. Fogg's cool manner toward Aouda. It

26
00:02:21.664 --> 00:02:27.534
was obvious to Passepartout that Aouda felt a deep gratitude to him for saving her life. Passepartout

27
00:02:27.535 --> 00:02:32.487
was beginning to think his master was quite heartless indeed. Aouda

28
00:02:32.488 --> 00:02:39.489
was also wondering how Mr. Fogg could remain so robot-like, even in her presence. As

29
00:02:39.490 --> 00:02:44.678
the Rangoon approached the end of its journey, the rough weather grew worse. The

30
00:02:44.679 --> 00:02:50.446
wind turned to blow from the northwest, and the steamer fell behind schedule. On

31
00:02:50.447 --> 00:02:54.805
November 3, a tempest tossed the steamer with a fury. The

32
00:02:54.806 --> 00:03:00.269
captain estimated that they would reach Hong Kong twenty hours behind schedule. Phileas

33
00:03:00.270 --> 00:03:06.609
Fogg stood at the ship's rail, gazing at the stormy sea with his usual tranquility. Aouda

34
00:03:06.610 --> 00:03:11.685
was amazed to find him as calm as the day she had first seen him. His

35
00:03:11.686 --> 00:03:20.642
expression didn't change, not for an instant, even though a delay of twenty hours would make him too late to catch the steamer to Yokohama. If

36
00:03:20.643 --> 00:03:25.061
he missed the steamer, he would likely lose his wager. Fix viewed

37
00:03:25.062 --> 00:03:27.856
the storm in a different light. Any delay

38
00:03:27.857 --> 00:03:31.966
would give the warrant more time to reach Hong Kong. And if

39
00:03:31.967 --> 00:03:38.548
Mr. Fogg missed the boat for Yokohama, he would be obliged to remain some days in Hong Kong. Passepartout, on

40
00:03:38.549 --> 00:03:43.947
the other hand, was enraged beyond expression by the difficult weather. Everything had

41
00:03:43.948 --> 00:03:47.180
gone so well until now! Throughout the

42
00:03:47.181 --> 00:03:51.896
worst of the wind, rain, and waves, he remained on deck, working with the crew, pitching in

43
00:03:51.897 --> 00:03:57.547
wherever he could to help the Rangoon 's progress through the storm. On

44
00:03:57.548 --> 00:04:04.406
November 4 the sea calmed, the wind turned favorable, and the steamer made good progress again. Land

45
00:04:04.407 --> 00:04:11.595
was sighted on the morning of November 6. They were 24 hours behind schedule. A

46
00:04:11.596 --> 00:04:19.600
harbor captain sailed out to meet the Rangoon , to guide its captain through the channels and islands around the port of Hong Kong.

47
00:04:19.601 --> 00:04:26.169
Mr. Fogg did not hesitate to approach the harbor captain and ask about the steamer to Yokohama.

48
00:04:26.170 --> 00:04:31.120
"The Carnatic leaves at high tide tomorrow morning," said the captain.

49
00:04:31.121 --> 00:04:37.827
"The steamer had to have one of its boilers repaired so its departure was postponed until tomorrow." "Ah,

50
00:04:37.828 --> 00:04:43.414
thank you," said Mr. Fogg, without betraying any astonishment. At

51
00:04:43.415 --> 00:04:46.743
one o'clock the Rangoon was at the quay. Mr.

52
00:04:46.744 --> 00:04:52.375
Fogg led Aouda to the Club Hotel and reserved a room for the young woman. After

53
00:04:52.376 --> 00:04:58.729
seeing that she had everything she needed, he set out in search of her wealthy relative, Jeejeeh. When

54
00:04:58.730 --> 00:05:03.141
Mr. Fogg returned to the hotel, he told her what he had learned. Mr.

55
00:05:03.142 --> 00:05:12.275
Jeejeeh had left China two years earlier. He had retired with his immense fortune and taken up residence in Holland. In

56
00:05:12.276 --> 00:05:17.193
her sweet, soft voice, Aouda asked, "What should I do, Mr. Fogg?" "It

57
00:05:17.194 --> 00:05:21.308
is very simple," he said. "Come to Europe." Aouda

58
00:05:21.309 --> 00:05:25.754
was surprised. "But I cannot intrude—" "You

59
00:05:25.755 --> 00:05:32.993
do not intrude, nor do you delay, my project in the least. Passepartout!" he called. "Monsieur?"

60
00:05:32.994 --> 00:05:35.487
said Passepartout. "Go

61
00:05:35.488 --> 00:05:41.945
to the Carnatic and reserve three cabins." Passepartout's

62
00:05:41.946 --> 00:05:47.008
Guidebook We have arrived in Hong Kong, and let me tell you, it is a bustling

63
00:05:47.009 --> 00:05:54.050
city! The name "Hong Kong" means "fragrant harbor," and its own harbor was once surrounded by flowering

64
00:05:54.051 --> 00:06:01.476
trees. Hong Kong consists of three main areas─Hong Kong Island, Kowloon Peninsula, and the New Territories.

65
00:06:01.477 --> 00:06:07.378
So Hong Kong is bigger than most people think, with 236 islands in total.

66
00:06:07.379 --> 00:06:13.759
In 1834 Britain attacked China and demanded the country give Hong Kong to Britain.

67
00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:18.037
China refused but did allow Britain to lease Hong Kong.

68
00:06:18.038 --> 00:06:23.498
I find that rather strange, don't you? A country being "rented" to another country?

69
00:06:23.499 --> 00:06:27.274
Maybe you're wondering why the British want Hong Kong for a colony.

70
00:06:27.275 --> 00:06:32.110
Well, it's mostly because Hong Kong is a massive trading port between East and West,

71
00:06:32.111 --> 00:06:40.648
and it acts as the gateway from America to Asia, and from Europe to Asia.

